.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt CMUS-REMOTE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmus-remote
.Nd control a running cmus
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl \-server Ar socket
.Op Fl lPqc
.Op Ar file ...
.Nm
.Op Fl \-server Ar socket
.Fl C Ar command ...
.Nm
.Op Fl \-server Ar socket
.Op Fl pusnrQ
.Op Fl v Ar volume
.Op Fl k Ar seek
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends commands to a running
.Xr cmus 1
through its socket and prints the answers.
It is installed in the GNU root.
With files, it adds them to the playlist, the library or the queue; with
.Fl C ,
each argument is a command as typed after a colon in
.Xr cmus 1 ;
with no arguments and no files, it reads commands from standard input, one
a line.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl \-server Ar socket
Connect to
.Ar socket
instead of the default, which
.Xr cmus 1
describes.
.It Fl p , Fl \-play
Start playing.
.It Fl u , Fl \-pause
Pause, or play again.
.It Fl s , Fl \-stop
Stop.
.It Fl n , Fl \-next
Play the next track.
.It Fl r , Fl \-prev
Play the track before.
.It Fl v , Fl \-volume Ar volume
Set the volume, as
.Ql 40% ,
or change it, as
.Ql +10% .
.It Fl k , Fl \-seek Ar seek
Seek to a time, as
.Ql 1:30 ,
or by an amount, as
.Ql +10 .
.It Fl f , Fl \-file Ar file
Play
.Ar file .
.It Fl Q
Print the status: whether a track plays, its file, its length and the
position in seconds, and every setting.
.It Fl l , Fl \-library
Add the files to the library.
.It Fl P , Fl \-playlist
Add the files to the playlist, as without an option.
.It Fl q , Fl \-queue
Add the files to the play queue.
.It Fl c , Fl \-clear
Empty the playlist, the library with
.Fl l ,
or the queue with
.Fl q ,
before adding.
.It Fl C , Fl \-raw
Send the arguments as commands.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It fails when no
.Xr cmus 1
answers on the socket.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run
.Xr cmus 1
in a
.Xr tmux 1
session of its own, play a file and read where it is:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
tmux new-session -d -s music cmus
cmus-remote -f ~/music/tone.flac
cmus-remote -Q | grep -E '^(status|position|duration)'
.Ed
.Pp
Set the volume, which is the PCM channel of
.Pa /dev/mixer :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cmus-remote -v 60%
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmus 1 ,
.Xr mixer 1
